On 25 September, Kipchoge won the [[2022 Berlin Marathon|Berlin Marathon]] decisively in a time of 2:01:09, beating by 30 seconds his own previous world record, which he set on the same course in 2018. With his fourth victory in Berlin, he equalled the record achievement of [[Haile Gebrselassie]]. He finished 4:49 min ahead of second-placed compatriot [[Mark Korir]] while Ethiopia's Tadu Abate took third place with a time of 2:06:28. Kipchoge achieved halfway in 59:51 which, being at the time, the fastest split in marathon history, would have been a world record in the standalone half-marathon in 1993, and was only 26 seconds off his best in that distance. He slowed down later with second half in 61:18.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/athletics/63025365 |language=en-GB |date=25 September 2022 |access-date=25 September 2022 |title=Eliud Kipchoge breaks his own marathon world record in Berlin |publisher=[[BBC News]] |archive-date=25 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220925093052/https://www.bbc.com/sport/athletics/63025365 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=25 September 2022 |title=Kipchoge breaks world record in Berlin with 2:01:09 |url=https://worldathletics.org
ews/report/eliud-kipchoge-world-record-berlin-marathon-2022 |access-date=25 September 2022 |website=[[World Athletics]] |archive-date=25 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220925100720/https://www.worldathletics.org
ews/report/eliud-kipchoge-world-record-berlin-marathon-2022 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=25 September 2022 |title=Eliud Kipchoge (2:01:09) Smashes World Record; Tigist Assefa (2:15:37) Stuns World at 2022 Berlin Marathon |url=https://www.letsrun.com
ews/2022/09/eliud-kipchoge-20109-smashes-world-record-tigist-assefa-21537-stuns-world-at-2022-berlin-marathon/ |access-date=25 September 2022 |website=[[LetsRun.com]] |language=en |archive-date=25 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220925095052/https://www.letsrun.com
ews/2022/09/eliud-kipchoge-20109-smashes-world-record-tigist-assefa-21537-stuns-world-at-2022-berlin-marathon/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Henderson |first=Jason |date=25 September 2022 |title=Eliud Kipchoge smashes world marathon record in Berlin |url=https://athleticsweekly.com/event-reports/eliud-kipchoge-smashes-world-marathon-record-in-berlin-1039961124/ |access-date=25 September 2022 |website=[[Athletics Weekly|AW]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=25 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220925105142/https://athleticsweekly.com/event-reports/eliud-kipchoge-smashes-world-marathon-record-in-berlin-1039961124/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It was the eighth time in a row that men's record was set in Berlin and 12th record there overall.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Schmitz |first=Rob |date=25 September 2022 |title=He was so fast, he had time to celebrate long before the second-place runner arrived |language=en |publisher=[[NPR]] |url=https://www.npr.org/2022/09/25/1124986817/eliud-kipchoge-world-record-berlin-marathon |access-date=27 September 2022 |archive-date=26 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220926212453/https://www.npr.org/2022/09/25/1124986817/eliud-kipchoge-world-record-berlin-marathon |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="BerlinRecords" />

